  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the best result so far at 0.485 acc, while scgpt (config_007, 0.411) underperforms and image-only resnet50 (config_010, 0.208) is very weak. The profile setting (single vs multi) is a critical, untested design axis that affects a large portion of the configuration space. Question: Does switching from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve upon the best singleprofile RNA result, while keeping the proven pca_n2000 encoder fixed? Why this is best: config_002 is a minimal, controlled change from config_001 (only profile setting and aggregation change), isolating the effect of multiprofile. Starting with avgpool (simpler aggregation) before transformer avoids confounding two new variables. The outcome directly informs whether to invest further experiments in multiprofile + transformer, multimodal multiprofile, or to abandon multiprofile altogether—making it the highest-information experiment under the limited budget."
